! fake-dom — reading TiddlyWiki's fake DOM out

`fake-dom.ts` owns ONE thing: the read-out of a tree TiddlyWiki already rendered. It builds no document and no element. TiddlyWiki ships its own fake DOM (`$tw.fakeDocument`, in `core/modules/utils/fakedom.js`); a camera renders into a container from that document, and this module converts the finished tree.

* ''`tw5ElementToVdom(container)`'' returns the container's children as `VDomNode[]` — an immutable tree of `element` nodes (`tagName`, `attrs`, `children`) and `text` nodes (`text`). An element's inline style, which the fake DOM keeps as a `_style` map, flattens back into one `style` attribute string.
* ''`tw5ElementToHtml(container)`'' returns the container's `innerHTML`, which TiddlyWiki's fake element builds natively. The island's projection reads the story surface through this call for each frame it posts (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/tw5-projection.ts`).
* ''The types'' `TW5FakeElement`, `TW5FakeTextNode` and `TW5FakeNode` name only the fields this module reads. The `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` flag tells an element from a text node at runtime.

''What it does not own.'' Listener storage, render-id stamping and the geometry and caret answers a live widget asks of a fake node belong to the projection, which patches the fake element's prototype. The converter reads a tree and changes nothing in it, and it needs a booted `$tw`.

